00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Say your prayers.

2
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Longlegs is a crime, horror, mystery film directed by Osgood Perkins.

3
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:15,000
FBI Agent Lee Harker is a gifted new recruit assigned to the
unsolved case of an elusive serial killer.

4
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:18,000
As the case takes complex turns, unearthing evidence of the occult, Harker discovers a personal connection to the
merciless killer and must race against time to stop him before he claims the lives of another innocent family.

5
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Agent Lee Harker, played by Maika Monroe.

6
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:24,000
Longlegs, played by Nicolas Cage.

7
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:27,000
Agent Carter, played by Blair Underwood.

8
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Ruth Harker, played by Alicia Witt.

9
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:33,000
Agent Browning, played by Michelle Choi-Lee.

10
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:36,000
Agent Fisk, played by Dakota Daulby.

11
00:55:33,000 --> 00:55:39,000
Longlegs is a 2024 American mystery horror thriller film
written and directed by Osgood Perkins.

12
01:00:36,000 --> 01:00:42,000
The film stars Maika Monroe, Blair Underwood, Alicia Witt, and Nicolas Cage.

13
01:05:39,000 --> 01:05:45,000
Set in the 1990s, the story follows a Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) agent assigned to hunt down an
occult-obsessed serial killer responsible for a string of family murders across Oregon.

14
01:10:42,000 --> 01:10:48,000
The killer is dubbed Longlegs, and baffles the FBI with his perfect ability to
seemingly leave zero trace of involvement at the crime scenes.

15
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:51,000
Cage served as a producer on the film through his
Saturn Films production company.

16
01:20:48,000 --> 01:20:54,000
Longlegs premiered in Los Angeles at the Grauman's Egyptian Theatre on July 8, 2024, and
was released theatrically in the United States by Neon on July 12, 2024.

17
01:25:51,000 --> 01:25:57,000
It received positive reviews and grossed $128 million worldwide on a budget of less than $10 million, becoming Neon's
highest-grossing film domestically, the highest-grossing independent film of the year, and Perkins's highest-grossing film.

18
01:30:54,000 --> 01:31:00,000
The film explores themes of homicide, fbi, religion
and supernatural, haunting, satanism.

19
01:35:57,000 --> 01:36:03,000
The tone is mind_bending and dark and thought_provoking.
